  "section": "3.5. Commercial General Liability (CGL)",
  "subsection": "E. Commercial General Liability (CGL) Insurance",
  "text": "For example: “Personal injury” may be defined to include: — “discrimination, racial or religious discrimination and/or violation of civil rights, humiliation, sexual discrimination, alienation of affection, however damages based on the above offenses are only covered where insurance against same is not prohibited by law.” [See Melugin v. Zurich Canada (1996) 50 CA4th 658, 663, 57 CR2d 781, 783] (a) [3:473] “Racial or religious discrimination” not applicable to employment discrimination: The terms “racial or religious discrimination” were held not to cover other forms of discrimination: e.g., employment discrimination (under Title VII of the 1964 Civil Rights Act or under the California FEHA). [American Motorists Ins. Co. v. Allied-Sysco Food Services, Inc., supra, 19 CA4th at 1349, 24 CR2d at 110 (disapproved on other grounds by Buss v. Sup.Ct. (Transamerica Ins.",
